# NestBridge Project Rules (CodeQuest 2026)

## What This Project Is
NestBridge is a culturally intelligent pairing platform connecting international
students, host families, local guides, and tourists. Group 21 — CodeQuest 2026.
Prototype reference: mellow-blini-a42359.netlify.app (29 screens total).

## Sprint Scope (Read Before Every Task)
- Bless may build, fix, or review ANY of the 29 screens — assignment lists show
  who builds first, not what is out of scope.
- Four high-priority demo screens: Search Hosts/Match Results, Host Profile &
  Pricing, Student Home Dashboard, SOS/Emergency Help.
- Matching algorithm, backend endpoints, Firebase wiring, and final navigation
  integration are Bless's responsibility regardless of who built individual screens.

## Core Technical Constraints
- Expo / React Native mobile app. Use TypeScript only (.ts / .tsx). No plain .js
  for new source files.
- ALWAYS use `StyleSheet.create()` for styling.
- STRICT RULE: Do NOT import or use external UI component libraries (e.g.,
  NativeBase, Tamagui, React Native Paper, Tailwind/NativeWind). Build raw layouts.
- Minimum touch target: 44×44pt for all interactive elements.

## Design System — Single Source of Truth
- ALL colors, fonts, spacing, and radii MUST come from `src/constants/theme.ts`.
- Import like: `import { colors, fontSizes, fontWeights, spacing, borderRadius, gradients } from '../constants/theme';`
- Never hardcode hex codes, arbitrary font sizes, or inline padding/margin values.
- Never duplicate brand colors in comments, rules, or components — if a token is
  missing, add it to `theme.ts` first, then use it.
- Semantic usage (enforced):
  * Header / splash gradients → gradients.header (navy → teal stops from theme)
  * CTAs / active states → colors.teal or colors.tealBright
  * Screen backgrounds → colors.background; warm panels → colors.warmCream
  * Cards / borders → colors.white with colors.border
  * Body text → colors.textPrimary; secondary → colors.textSecondary; muted → colors.textTertiary
  * SOS and errors → colors.danger; pending / stars → colors.warning (verify gold vs prototype)
  * Confirmed / paid → colors.success; highlight accents → colors.gold or colors.terracotta (verify first)

## Component Architecture
- EVERY screen is a pure, presentational default-export function component.
- ALL displayed data MUST arrive via props — never hardcode or generate content
  inside the screen component.
- Typed props: define a `Props` interface (or type) for every screen.

## Data — Two Phases (Both Valid)
**Phase 1 — Presentational screens (current sprint default)**
- Screen receives data only through props.
- Parent files, Storybook-style previews, or test harnesses pass sample/mock
  datasets to verify layout. Mock data lives OUTSIDE the screen file.
- This is how parallel teammates build isolated screens before integration.

**Phase 2 — Integrated app (Bless's wiring pass)**
- Screens fetch via `src/services/api.js` (Axios). No inline fetch(), no second
  HTTP client.
- Do not mock API calls in production navigation paths — hit the real backend.
- If the backend is unreachable, show a clear error state, not silent placeholder data.
- Loading: ActivityIndicator while fetching. Never show a blank screen.

## Product UX Rules (Non-Negotiable)
- SOS floating button must never be hidden, covered, or removed on any screen.
- Match results must show: compatibility %, trust badge, and ≥2 plain-English
  match reasons.
- Booking screen must show: nightly rate + platform fee + total + cancellation
  policy before the pay CTA.
- Onboarding: one primary decision per screen. KYC and photo upload always offer
  a soft skip ("Verify later" / "Skip for now").
- Pre-fill search from onboarding context (destination, dates) when available.

## Multimodal / Prototype Matching
- If the user attaches a screenshot from the Netlify prototype, match that layout
  structure cleanly while strictly using `theme.ts` tokens — never approximate colors
  from the screenshot.

## Project Layout
- `src/screens/` — one file per screen (auth, onboarding, student, host, guide,
  tourist, shared)
- `src/constants/theme.ts` — design tokens (do not create colors.js)
- `frontend/` — Expo app entry (migrate to TypeScript as integration proceeds)
- `docs/AGENTS.md` — full architecture reference (navigation, Firebase, API)
